      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A mononuclear tantallacyclopentadiene complex, TaCl3(C4H2tBu2) (3), serves as a unique ligand to nickel: the addition of Ni(COD)2 to 3 selectively afforded heterobimetallic Ta-Ni complex 4. The cyclooctadiene ligand bound to the nickel center in complex 4 was readily substituted by monodentate and bidentate phosphine ligands, such as dimethylphenylphosphine, 1,2-bis(diphenylphosphino)ethane, and 1,2-bis(diethylphosphino)ethane, to give the corresponding phosphine complexes 5, 6a, and 6b. We also examined a ligand substitution reaction with 1,3-bis(2,6-diisopropylphenyl)imidazol-2-ylidene (IPr) to produce the corresponding Ta-Ni complex 7. These newly prepared Ta-Ni heterobimetallic complexes were characterized spectroscopically together with the crystal structures of 4, 6a, and 7."},
